/*****************************************************************************
    jitJ6 -- RUNG 6 OF THE jitLadder. 2026-07-31.   J5 + AN EMITTED CALL.

    ⚠ THE FIRST EMITTED CALL IN THIS LAYER THAT IS NOT THE LONELY concatEQ, and
    the mechanism under FOUR separate threads: the fallback column (every
    non-scalar type's path), jitTrace (the debugging story), J-R (recursion, and
    behind it the frame model), and the runtime surface that makes the whole
    language reachable from compiled code. One arc, four doors.

    THE CLAIM THIS RUNG ADDS: a call is EMITTED INTO the function and RUNS AT
    RUN TIME, once per fire -- not executed during compilation.

    ⚠ AND THE TRACE ITSELF IS THE EVIDENCE, which is why this rung asserts
    something no previous rung could. `print` cannot do this job: opPrint is
    UNGATED, so a print inside a jitted body fires at EMIT time (jit.md S2.2,
    measured) -- it reports COMPILE-TIME state ONCE and looks like it worked.
    A trace that appears TWICE, with DIFFERENT VALUES, can only have been called
    from compiled code on each fire.

        fire 1   jfIn = 4   ->  trace prints 4,  jfOut = 8
        fire 2   jfIn = 11  ->  trace prints 11, jfOut = 22   NO RECOMPILE

    DIAGNOSTIC, per rung style:
        two traces, 4 then 11   correct -- emitted, run at run time, per fire
        ONE trace                the call ran at EMIT time (the print disease)
        two traces, both 4       the argument was folded, not loaded per fire
        no trace at all          nothing was emitted

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (standing harness rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitLadder6);
define
    jfIn;
    jfOut;
    jitJ6 code={
        jitTrace(jfIn);
        jfOut = jfIn * 2;
        };
    ;

jfIn  = 4;
jfOut = 0;
print "J6 fire 1 setup : jfIn =" jfIn:;
testing(jitJ6);
print "J6 fire 1 result: jfOut =" jfOut " (want 8)":;

jfIn  = 11;
jfOut = 0;
print "J6 fire 2 setup : jfIn =" jfIn " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "J6 fire 2 result: jfOut =" jfOut " (want 22)":;

jfIn  = 4;
jfOut = 0;
jitJ6();
print "J6 interpreted  : jfOut =" jfOut " (the oracle -- want 8)":;

print "J6 SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
